WEBVTT

00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:17,460
How many here have food sensitivities?

00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:20,460
How about gluten sensitivity?

00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:23,740
Why would anybody have a gluten sensitivity?

00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:27,020
Gluten is gliadin, which is the protein

00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,900
of wheat, rye, barley, malt, spelt.

00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,660
That should go into the body.

00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:34,660
And what happens?

00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:39,700
So you have this protein, part of it's digested with HCl.

00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:42,100
Most of it's digested with your digestive enzymes

00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:44,580
that you're first part of a small intestine.

00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:47,340
It should be cleaved into very small pieces

00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,940
called amino acids.

00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:51,620
So if you think of a protein, a protein

00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:55,620
is a long chain of amino acids in a certain configuration.

00:00:55,620 --> 00:00:58,580
If you think of it as a beaded necklace,

00:00:58,580 --> 00:00:59,780
that's the protein.

00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:04,060
And gliadin is a certain protein because of the certain sequence

00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,380
of amino acids that are in that chain.

00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:08,980
Now as you digest that beaded necklace,

00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:11,060
your digestive enzymes should break off

00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:14,020
like little snippers, all those amino acids

00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:17,180
and into just single beads of amino acids.

00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:18,580
Now it's not gliadin anymore.

00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:20,340
It's not gluten anymore.

00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:23,180
It's simply an amino acid.

00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:27,580
That amino acid is supposed to cross the gut barrier.

00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:32,140
Problem is is that if I have a damaged gut barrier,

00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:35,220
I have gaps between the cells.

00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:40,180
Now before it's completely cleaved into individual amino acids,

00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:42,860
there's a strand of 12, there's a strand of 8th,

00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:45,780
there's a strand of 15, there's a strand of 35.

00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:49,300
These are able to get across the gut.

00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:51,060
They get across the gut and remember,

00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:54,180
if it's still in the gut, it's not really in your body.

00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:55,300
Think of it that way.

00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,740
Now it's in your body.

00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:59,420
And it's in the bloodstream and your immune system

00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:04,820
goes, what in the world is that thing?

00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:06,580
And what does your immune system do?

00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:08,740
Your immune system doesn't escort it out of the body.

00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:11,780
Your immune system does one thing and it doesn't really well.

00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:13,660
It kills things.

00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:15,820
So it goes, what in the world is that?

00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:18,500
I know, let's kill it.

00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:22,020
So it kills that thing.

00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:25,020
So well, you can't really kill a protein.

00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:26,340
Now it's a peptide.

00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:28,020
So you can't really kill that peptide.

00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:31,260
So it starts to make antibodies against that peptide.

00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:33,180
And now we have a food sensitivity.

00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:35,820
So now everywhere you see that peptide,

00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:38,980
also inside the gut, when you eat gluten,

00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:43,740
you fire this in immune reaction and you cause this state

00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:46,500
of inflammation, which does what?

00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:50,940
Further damage is the epithelial lining of the gut.

00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:54,020
So it is, that's why we have food sensitivities.

00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:58,780
We have food sensitivities because those foods in partial form

00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,540
never should have got across the gut in the first place.

00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:05,940
So you could say, if we didn't ever have damage to the gut,

00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:08,340
would we be dealing with food sensitivities?

00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:10,860
The answer is not nearly at the percentage

00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:12,460
that we're dealing with them though.

00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:14,260
Why is this rise of food sensitivities?

00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:16,260
My goodness, everybody's going to burn out.

00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:18,060
There must be a bad, right?

00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:21,540
No, it's because everybody's got damaged guts.

00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:24,380
And whether that's a fat or not, it's the truth.

00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:26,340
And it's because we live in a world that

00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:29,380
we're surrounded by chemicals that we're not

00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:33,380
supposed to be exposed to, no matter how good you try to live

00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:35,620
or you're going to be a guru and move to a mountaintop.

00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:36,740
You can't get away from it.

00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:38,820
It's going to damage your gut wall.

00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:40,660
When you have damage to the gut wall, things

00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:42,700
are going to get through that never should have got through.

00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:45,660
So go back to, should I eat mercury in fish?

00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:48,380
Well, knowing how my gut is, I better not

00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:52,180
be eating any mercury because it's going to probably absorb.

00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:54,900
And I'm going to have problems.

00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:56,020
Does that make sense?

